{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One day Jason finishes his math homework early, and decides to take a jog through his neighborhood. While jogging, Jason trips over a leprechaun. After dusting himself off and apologizing to the odd little magical creature, Jason, thinking there is nothing unusual about the situation, starts jogging again. Immediately the leprechaun calls out, \"hey, stupid, this is your only chance to win gold from a leprechaun!\"\nJason, while not particularly greedy, recognizes the value of gold. Thinking about his limited college savings, Jason approaches the leprechaun and asks about the opportunity. The leprechaun hands Jason a fair coin and tells him to clop it as many times as it takes to flip a head. For each tail Jason flips, the leprechaun promises one gold coin.\nIf Jason flips a head right away, he wins nothing. If he first flips a tail, then a head, he wins one gold coin. If he's lucky and flips ten tails before the first head, he wins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5dfc22d26fd95948dc4c2ec660f75e55f896dca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{ten gold coins.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" /> What is the expected number of gold coins Jason wins at this game?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f33a9c105aff1c1e291d921062115fdd92f6b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac1{10}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac18\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac15\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac14\\qquad \\textbf{(F) }\\dfrac13\\qquad \\textbf{(G) }\\dfrac25\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"539\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f33bb15c51ee52c3c153c4903118059339eb8f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(H) }\\dfrac12\\qquad \\textbf{(I) }\\dfrac35\\qquad \\textbf{(J) }\\dfrac23\\qquad \\textbf{(K) }\\dfrac45\\qquad \\textbf{(L) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(M) }\\dfrac54\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"443\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2ead03744b89ab55508e768b805fb9eb66c255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(N) }\\dfrac43\\qquad \\textbf{(O) }\\dfrac32\\qquad \\textbf{(P) }2\\qquad \\textbf{(Q) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(R) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(S) }2007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"464\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability of getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> head is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  The probability of getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tail then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> head is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  From there, the probability of getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> tails then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> head is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43eb25f80ff62093367a265c72f88b0b435622fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{n+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be expected value of earnings.  Using expected value,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023baa75aff708b8fb8a3f2d713e52c847a15909.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = 0 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{16} \\cdots\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5b861fe43c88747d072b011f8f85829e93be14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2E = 0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdots\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"37\" />\nSubtract original to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/8609fd03ecc465b7d5178613bf071e25702b8e0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdots\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"37\" />\nUsing the infinite series formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc452efdc6b60d60ce2ad2cf40feff656326f05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"117\" height=\"47\" />, so Jason is expected to earn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc3ffe46e68b0c49da55f0475505c9b9d00a26a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(L) } 1 \\text{ gold coin}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"126\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 iTest Pro